Run
/ Runs the goal Claude wrote, %goal% (the whole goal: its name, then its steps): saved in the person's app
/ (/agent/run/Run.goal), built, and run in a plang of its own — no link to the host, the person's own permissions.
/ What it wrote and its exit code; or, when it doesn't build, what the build said.
- file.save(Path="/agent/run/Run.goal", Value=%goal%)
- terminal.start(App="plang", Parameter=["build", "agent/run/Run.goal"]); on.timeout(After="PT2M"); variable.set(Name=%built%, Value=%!data%)
- condition.if(Left=%built!exitCode%, Operator="!=", Right=0) { goal.call(Name="NotBuilt") }
- terminal.start(App="plang", Parameter=["agent/run/Run"]); on.timeout(After="PT5M"); variable.set(Name=%ran%, Value=%!data%)
- return {output: %ran%, error: %ran!error%, code: %ran!exitCode%}

NotBuilt
/ out of Run too (depth 2): what didn't build is the answer, nothing runs
- goal.return(Data={built: false, output: %built%, error: %built!error%, code: %built!exitCode%}, Depth=2)
